          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 136,
          "start": 472.05,
          "end": 476.67,
          "en": "later in the course, once we start sending HTTP requests,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 137,
          "start": 476.67,
          "end": 480.09,
          "en": "we'll encounter Observables that are done",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 138,
          "start": 480.09,
          "end": 483.09,
          "en": "after a response has been received.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 139,
          "start": 483.09,
          "end": 485.67,
          "en": "So it is possible that you have Observables",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 140,
          "start": 485.67,
          "end": 488.88,
          "en": "that should not keep on running forever.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 141,
          "start": 488.88,
          "end": 492.03,
          "en": "Interval and also my custom interval here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 142,
          "start": 492.03,
          "end": 493.71,
          "en": "are running forever,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 143,
          "start": 493.71,
          "end": 496.38,
          "en": "but it doesn't have to be like that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 144,
          "start": 496.38,
          "end": 500.31,
          "en": "For example, here in my customerInterval Observable,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 145,
          "start": 500.31,
          "end": 504.3,
          "en": "I could add a variable count",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 146,
          "start": 504.3,
          "end": 508.47,
          "en": "or timesExecuted, whatever,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 147,
          "start": 508.47,
          "end": 510.153,
          "en": "which is 0 initially.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 148,
          "start": 511.05,
          "end": 514.53,
          "en": "And then here, whenever I emit a new value,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 149,
          "start": 514.53,
          "end": 519.243,
          "en": "I increment timesExecute like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 150,
          "start": 521.43,
          "end": 523.573,
          "en": "And I then check at the beginning",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 151,
          "start": 523.573,
          "end": 527.88,
          "en": "if timesExecuted is greater than five, let's say",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 152,
          "start": 527.88,
          "end": 531.753,
          "en": "or three, maybe two, reach that point a bit earlier.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 153,
          "start": 532.71,
          "end": 537.69,
          "en": "And if that's the case, I actually wanna clear that interval",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 154,
          "start": 537.69,
          "end": 540.87,
          "en": "and also complete that Observable",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 155,
          "start": 540.87,
          "end": 542.82,
          "en": "to clean up the subscription",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 156,
          "start": 542.82,
          "end": 547.083,
          "en": "and to make it clear that no new values will be emitted.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 157,
          "start": 548.49,
          "end": 550.05,
          "en": "Now I can clear the interval",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 158,
          "start": 550.05,
          "end": 553.77,
          "en": "by storing this interval ID in the end",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 159,
          "start": 553.77,
          "end": 555.69,
          "en": "in some constant or variable",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 160,
          "start": 555.69,
          "end": 559.59,
          "en": "because setInterval does return such an identifier.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 161,
          "start": 559.59,
          "end": 563.79,
          "en": "And then here in the if statement, I can call clearInterval",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 162,
          "start": 563.79,
          "end": 568.47,
          "en": "and clear it like this using some standard JavaScript code.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 163,
          "start": 568.47,
          "end": 572.05,
          "en": "So this has nothing to do with RxJS",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 164,
          "start": 573.39,
          "end": 578.193,
          "en": "and I can also use my subscriber to call complete.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 165,
          "start": 579.45,
          "end": 581.43,
          "en": "And with that I'll emit an event",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 166,
          "start": 581.43,
          "end": 584.19,
          "en": "that will automatically clean up the subscription",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 167,
          "start": 584.19,
          "end": 585.9,
          "en": "and that will make it clear",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 168,
          "start": 585.9,
          "end": 588.543,
          "en": "that there will be no future values.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 169,
          "start": 589.62,
          "end": 591.363,
          "en": "And then here I'll return.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 170,
          "start": 594.63,
          "end": 597.99,
          "en": "Now you can also listen to that complete event",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 171,
          "start": 597.99,
          "end": 599.853,
          "en": "when setting up a subscription.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 172,
          "start": 600.81,
          "end": 602.37,
          "en": "In that observer object here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 173,
          "start": 602.37,
          "end": 605.7,
          "en": "you cannot just define a function that should be executed",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 174,
          "start": 605.7,
          "end": 607.53,
          "en": "if a new value is emitted.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 175,
          "start": 607.53,
          "end": 609.63,
          "en": "So when the next event occurs,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 176,
          "start": 609.63,
          "end": 612.03,
          "en": "but you can also set up a complete function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 177,
          "start": 612.03,
          "end": 615.513,
          "en": "that will be triggered when the Observable completes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 178,
          "start": 616.56,
          "end": 619.53,
          "en": "So here we could say 'COMPLETED!\"",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 179,
          "start": 619.53,
          "end": 620.673,
          "en": "And log that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 180,
          "start": 622.26,
          "end": 625.59,
          "en": "If you do that and you reload,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 181,
          "start": 625.59,
          "end": 629.82,
          "en": "you'll see that we, again, start emitting values",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 182,
          "start": 629.82,
          "end": 632.34,
          "en": "that works like before,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 183,
          "start": 632.34,
          "end": 636.483,
          "en": "but then at some point we'll get completed.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 184,
          "start": 638.04,
          "end": 640.95,
          "en": "Essentially we get this as soon",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 185,
          "start": 640.95,
          "end": 643.89,
          "en": "as the timesExecuted variable",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 186,
          "start": 643.89,
          "end": 647.01,
          "en": "has a value greater than three, so at least four.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 187,
          "start": 647.01,
          "end": 650.28,
          "en": "That's why we get four logs here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 188,
          "start": 650.28,
          "end": 654.243,
          "en": "and then it's completed and no new values are emitted.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 189,
          "start": 655.41,
          "end": 659.19,
          "en": "And that's therefore also something Observables can do,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 190,
          "start": 659.19,
          "end": 663.57,
          "en": "both built-in Observables or Observables offered by Angular",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 191,
          "start": 663.57,
          "end": 666.243,
          "en": "and Observables, you might be building on your own.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 192,
          "start": 667.98,
          "end": 670.89,
          "en": "And last but not least, it's also worth knowing",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 193,
          "start": 670.89,
          "end": 675.15,
          "en": "that the Observables can also throw an error.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 194,
          "start": 675.15,
          "end": 677.34,
          "en": "You can emit an error event,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 195,
          "start": 677.34,
          "end": 679.863,
          "en": "which can carry some error data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 196,
          "start": 680.76,
          "end": 682.56,
          "en": "Now I don't need that here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 197,
          "start": 682.56,
          "end": 685.74,
          "en": "but if you had some logic wrapped in an Observable",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 198,
          "start": 685.74,
          "end": 690.45,
          "en": "that could fail, you might wanna emit such an error value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 199,
          "start": 690.45,
          "end": 693.12,
          "en": "because of course, when setting up that observer,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 200,
          "start": 693.12,
          "end": 697.08,
          "en": "you can also define an error function that will be triggered",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 201,
          "start": 697.08,
          "end": 699.3,
          "en": "whenever an error occurs.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 202,
          "start": 699.3,
          "end": 701.463,
          "en": "That is also possible.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 203,
          "start": 703.26,
          "end": 707.22,
          "en": "And that's therefore how you can create custom Observables",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 204,
          "start": 707.22,
          "end": 712.14,
          "en": "and how these Observables interact with these observers",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 205,
          "start": 712.14,
          "end": 715.62,
          "en": "that you pass to these subscribe functions.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 206,
          "start": 715.62,
          "end": 719.55,
          "en": "In the end, it's this observer object that's received",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 207,
          "start": 719.55,
          "end": 722.79,
          "en": "as an input in this function that's passed",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 208,
          "start": 722.79,
          "end": 725.28,
          "en": "to the Observable constructor.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 209,
          "start": 725.28,
          "end": 728.76,
          "en": "And you can then control when exactly,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 210,
          "start": 728.76,
          "end": 732.93,
          "en": "so at which point of time which event is triggered.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 211,
          "start": 732.93,
          "end": 737.28,
          "en": "So when exactly which observer function here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 212,
          "start": 737.28,
          "end": 738.84,
          "en": "will be executed.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 213,
          "start": 738.84,
          "end": 741.993,
          "en": "That's how Observables work under the hood.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}
